---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Community — Agent Toolkit"
  description="Contribute to Agent Toolkit, get help, report a security issue or explore the Agentic Harness reference workspace."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source · built in the open</p>
      <h1>Find your way into the project.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agent Toolkit owns the runtime, engine and Desktop. Contributions and
        support happen in the same repository that builds the product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--deep" style="padding-top: 24px">
    <div class="wrap community-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit">
        <strong>Source repository ↗</strong>
        <span>Browse the code, current releases and active work.</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit/issues">
        <strong>Issues and requests ↗</strong>
        <span>Report a problem or propose a capability.</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
        <strong>Contribute ↗</strong>
        <span>Read the canonical contributor guide.</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit/blob/main/SECURITY.md">
        <strong>Security ↗</strong>
        <span>
          Report vulnerabilities through the project's disclosure process.
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--glow">
    <div class="wrap scene-grid">
      <div class="scene-copy">
        <p class="section-kicker">A reference workspace, not a second engine</p>
        <h2>See how a complete workspace can be composed.</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agentic-harness">
            Agentic Harness
          </a>{" "}
          is a persistent example workspace with its own knowledge, packs,
          personas and project index. It demonstrates how to compose Agent
          Toolkit in a real environment; Agent Toolkit remains the canonical
          runtime and capability owner.
        </p>
        <a
          class="quiet-link"
          href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agentic-harness"
        >
          Explore the Harness <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="closing-banner">
        <p class="section-kicker">Three clean responsibilities</p>
        <h3>
          Toolkit runs.
          <br />
          Harness composes.
          <br />
          Projects get the work.
        </h3>
        <p>
          Keep runtime, workspace and project configuration in their proper
          homes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
